<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed secondary market participation whereby it had sought to drain 4.100 billion pesos from the system on Wednesday, through a combination of three direct sales of paper combined with eight repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    344 days   23.75 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days   22.65 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days   22.02 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     51 days   21.75 pct</p>
<p>    450 million     37 days   20.80 pct</p>
<p>    350 million     36 days   20.89 pct</p>
<p>    750 million     29 days   20.81 pct</p>
<p>    350 million     22 days   20.43 pct</p>
<p>    350 million     15 days   20.04 pct</p>
<p>    800 million	7 days   19.99 pct</p>
<p>    200 million	1 day    19.65 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
